* ==================================================================
* tb_dr0014_sampling_extracted -- issue #89 Sec 6.3: the DR-0012/13
* Gain-error-systematic row (Group A, terms 1+2 + sampling gain/INL)
* and the C_par-mismatch residue (Group C, term 4), against the
* PMOS-body-remediated, MiM-mapped EXTRACTED ADC_TOP core, on
* sim/dr0014-sampling/'s own schedule and LSB-referred formulas.
*
* GENERATED by
* layout/adc-top/parasitics/gen_extracted_dr0014_sampling_tb.py --
* do not edit.
*
* Group B (fourth-leg settling A/B) and Group D (isolated T-gate
* R_on) have no extracted equivalent -- see this generator's own
* module docstring for why -- and are not emitted here.
* ==================================================================

* ---- retained waveforms --------------------------------------------
* ngspice keeps a transient waveform for EVERY node unless told which
* ones matter, and this deck instantiates the in-path-extracted core
* EIGHT times (five Group A pairs + three Group C), so every leg node
* the star-split adds is paid for eight times over. Measured at
* tt_27c_3.30v: 1378.5 MB peak RSS without this line, 158.3 MB with
* it -- 8.7x. The 1.4 GB form still completed on a quiet host, so the
* honest statement is not 'it cannot run' but 'nine of these at the
* -j 9 this 27 point grid is run at want ~12 GB of waveform store' --
* the same load-dependent failure that killed every INL/DNL point in
* PR #130. These are exactly the vectors
* sim/dr0014-sampling/testbench-extracted/tb.json reads, derived from
* it rather than hand-listed. Retention only: no model, tolerance or
* timestep changes, and all 43 measurements are bit-identical with and
* without it. See gen_extracted_core_tb.saved_vectors_lines.
.save v(a0_dd) v(a0_dn) v(a0_dp) v(a1_dd) v(a1_dn) v(a1_dp) v(a2_dd) v(a2_dn) v(a2_dp) v(a3_dd) v(a3_dn) v(a3_dp) v(a4_dd) v(a4_dn) v(a4_dp) v(c0_dd) v(c0_dn) v(c0_dp) v(c1_dd) v(c1_dn) v(c1_dp) v(c2_dd) v(c2_dn) v(c2_dp)

.param vref={vdd_val}
.param vcm={vdd_val/2}
.param lsb={vdd_val/1024}
.param ibias=10u

* ---- rails ---------------------------------------------------------
vddd vddd 0 dc {vdd_val}
vddc vddc 0 dc {vdd_val}
vrefs vrefn 0 dc {vref}
vcms vcmn 0 dc {vcm}
* Comparator strobe held LOW throughout, same rationale as the
* schematic deck: the latch is in reset/preamp-tracking while a DAC
* step settles; kickback on the strobe edge is sim/comparator-kickback/.
vcmpstrobe cmpstrobe 0 dc 0

